opennyai_summary.facts:
The present criminal revision has been filed to quash the order dated 05.7.2024, passed by Court of Juvenile Justice Board, Kaushambi, in bail aplication no.40/2024, (State of U.P. Versus MABT),
Case Crime no.35 of 2024, under section 363, 366, 376(3), 342, 506 1.P.C. and section 3/4 of protection of Children from Sexual offences Act, & section 3(2)5 of scheduled castes and scheduled tribes (prevention of atrocities) Act, P.S. - Kokhraj, District - Kaushambi, by which the Court of Juvenile Justice Board, Kaushambi had rejected bail application of revisionist and learned Juvenile Child In Conflict With Law Mabt vs State Of U.P. And 3 Others on 10 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/147806424/
1 Court/Special Judge (POCSO), Kaushambi.
Learned counsel for the revisionist submits:
(i) admittedly, the revisionist was a juvenile on the date of alleged incident being 16 years, 09 months and 11 days of age; he is in child protection home since 11.03.2024.
(ii) the revisionist has been falsely implicated;
(iii) there is no specific or strong objection raised in the DPO report, other than the general and vague observations;
(iv) there is no criminal history of the revisionist;
(v) there is no hope of early conclusion of the trial;
(vi) the revisionist has remained confined in the child observation home for an unduly long period of time;
(vii) none of the grounds contemplated under section 12 of the Juvenile Justice (Care and Protection of Children) Act, 2000 (hereinafter referred to as the Act) are available, to deny the bail to the revisionist.
(ix) therefore, the impugned orders have been assailed as erroneous and contrary to law.
